1
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
A twenty-first century portrait.

2
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Vox Lux is a drama, music film directed by Brady Corbet.

3
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
In 1999, teenage sisters Celeste and Eleanor survive a seismic, violent tragedy.

4
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:26,000
The sisters compose and perform a song about their experience, making something lovely and
cathartic out of catastrophe — while also catapulting Celeste to stardom.

5
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
By 2017, the now 31-year-old Celeste is mother to a teenage daughter of her own and struggling to navigate a
career fraught with scandals when another act of terrifying violence demands her attention.

6
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Celeste Montgomery, played by Natalie Portman.

7
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Young Celeste / Albertine, played by Raffey Cassidy.

8
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Manager, played by Jude Law.

9
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Eleanor "Ellie" Montgomery, played by Stacy Martin.

10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Josie, played by Jennifer Ehle.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
Journalist, played by Christopher Abbott.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Vox Lux is a 2018 American musical drama film written and directed by
Brady Corbet, from a story by Corbet and Mona Fastvold.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film stars Natalie Portman, Jude Law, Raffey
Cassidy, Stacy Martin and Jennifer Ehle.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Vox Lux had its world premiere at the 75th Venice International Film Festival on September
4, 2018, and was released in the United States on December 7, 2018, by Neon.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
The film received generally favorable reviews from film critics,
and grossed $1.4 million on an $11 million budget.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of pop star, icon, school shooting, 1990s, 2000s.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The tone is dark and emotional.
